{
  "about": [
    "The quiz data of images/japan-quiz: the single source of truth for the prefectures, islands and regions, their names and readings. tools/build_map.py reads it; the geometry fix-ups live there (tools/README.md).",
    "prefectures: JIS order (iso = ISO 3166-2:JP). id: the prefecture's answer id and the id of its main map piece (<path> in site/map.svg); parts off its main island form a second piece <id>-isles. Okinawa is one piece (island null).",
    "name, capital: Hepburn with macrons. kanji: the name without the generic suffix (県, 府, 都), whole where the suffix is part of the name (北海道); kana: its hiragana reading. capital_kanji / capital_kana: the same for the capital without 市 / 区 (Saitama's capital is written さいたま). Tōkyō's capital is Shinjuku (seat of the metropolitan government).",
    "capital_differs: the capital's name differs from the prefecture's (the capitals round asks these 18; Tōkyō counts).",
    "region: one of the eight standard regions (Mie in Kansai, Okinawa in Kyūshū). island: the main island its main piece lies on.",
    "ne_name: Natural Earth's name for the feature matched by iso (ne_10m_admin_1_states_provinces, iso_3166_2); build_map.py checks it.",
    "Kanji and kana were cross-checked against Wikidata (labels, P1814 name in kana), the Japanese Wikipedia articles and English Wikipedia's List of regions of Japan; build_map.py checks every kana reading against its Hepburn name."
  ],
